    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_902958a6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman in a revealing outfit leaning into a car at night, with overlaid text that reads: 'i think it's funny to haggle overprice with with hookers when you're just going to kill them anyway.' The scene is framed to suggest a transactional or predatory interaction. The text explicitly uses the term 'hookers,' which is a derogatory and dehumanizing label for sex workers, and implies violence ('just going to kill them anyway'), which is both threatening and misogynistic. The meme's intent is to normalize or joke about the violent potential of interactions with sex workers, reducing their humanity and dignity. This aligns with misogynous toxicity as it objectifies women, frames them as disposable or expendable, and promotes a violent, predatory mindset toward them. The juxtaposition of the visual (a woman in a suggestive outfit) with the text (a violent, transactional threat) reinforces the harmful stereotype that women in sex work are inherently dangerous or deserving of violence, which is a form of misogynistic hate.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_da5de142"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
